# The built APKs are attached to GitHub Releases by CI, not committed. Binaries in git are
# never garbage collected: every build would stay in the repository's history forever, and a
# clone would grow by ~10MB per release for files nobody reads from there anyway.
releases/*.apk

# Signing material must never be committed. The keystore lives outside every repository, and
# losing it means these apps can never be updated again.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.b64
*.b64.txt
keystore.properties
